If you're getting complaints about things not being commands when you
try to patch, it's probably not Nethack that's the problem, but rather
MinGW.  Whenever it complains about a missing program/command, figure
out where that program is in the mingw directory tree and make sure
that subdirectory is in your PATH.  How exactly you do that depends
on your operating system.



